en  the head of the family  Lawrence ended up with a cold they  thought it was just a cold and then when  it got progressively worse in three days  and on the fourth day you're going to  the hospital they didn't expect for him  to be dead by the fifth so I just have  to say it's taking people out it's real  and this is what I want to say to our  community in particular because I think  people now are hearing the message  because media is now putting this on  high alert for for all people and black  people to understand that it affects us  if their pre-existing conditions but I  think people aren't still getting the  message that it's not just the people  who you see have it or you think might  have it it's the people who are  asymptomatic it's why in my own house  one of my beloved daughters from South  Africa wanted to come home from Stanford  and I said he can't come because there's  no way for me to get you here you can't  take a train not gonna be on a bus not  gonna be on a plane opening yourself up  to everybody their only way you can come  is that can send security to get you and  then you put security in danger cuz I  don't know where you've been or who  you've been around and so that daughter  is still living alone in her own  apartment and we all FaceTime every  night but I didn't let her come into the  to the space be just because I thought  even if you endanger one other person  who has to come and get you so it's not  not the people who you know have it who  were sneezing and aches and pains it's  the people who perhaps are asymptomatic  and at the beginning of the series I had  the pleasure of interviewing a jurist  and his wife who were in quarantine in  in New Mexico never did they show a  symptom ever  they were asymptomatic and never through  the hole to two weeks quarantine and  then after did they ever show a symptom  so I think it's all of these people who  perhaps could be carriers and then  bringing it into your home so it's not  just I want to say to folks not just  isolating your stuff but don't let  anybody else come in your house right  and you you're it so a couple of points  that you just made that I want to sort  of focus on you talked about Milwaukee  and what we've seen a really distressing  statistic that we've seen replicated  over and over again is in cities and in  states where black people are not the  majority they are disproportionately  affected by coab in nineteen seventy  percent of the deaths in chicago our  black americans yet they only make up  30% of the population and you spoke to  their glory light but what did she tell  you well she told me that you know the  same thing i think that she shared at  that news conference only she spoken in  depth about the numbers just take your  breath away and how difficult it is when  you are living in housing where you have  no way of getting away from the rest of  the people in the house except to close  off a room and put yourself in a room  how social distancing in the  african-american community is far more  difficult in the african-american and  brown community because you have more  people living in the home and I talked  to a minister on the south side of  Chicago for this series who lost his  sister and his best friend since high  school within the same couple of days  Dudek ovid wasn't able to be with either  of them at the end and wasn't even able  to have a funeral I think that's what  people don't understand is that it's  taking people out the family in  Milwaukee told me they couldn't believe  that in five days their family member  was gone they're still looking at the  chair that he held everything sat in and  every night in the living room you just  can't believe they're sharing with me  that we hear 14 days they thought they  had 14 days because you don't have 14  days if the virus hits it hits your  lungs you're out you're gone and so for  those who can't recover particularly  with pre-existing conditions and all the  people I 